WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:04.040
You probably recognize Rick Petko from American
Chopper.

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:08.769
He started working at Orange County Choppers
as a fabricator and builder in July 2003,

00:00:08.769 --> 00:00:11.200
but he's not part of the operation anymore.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.360
So, what's Petko up to these days?

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:14.549
He got married in 2012

00:00:14.549 --> 00:00:18.860
In 2012, Petko married Brittany Cockeram on
an episode of American Chopper.

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:23.030
Even though Senior and Junior were feuding
at the time, they still came out for Petko's

00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:24.030
wedding.

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:26.410
Once Petko was married, his priorities began
to shift.

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:31.360
Petko and Cockeram welcomed their first daughter,
Everly Rose, in October 2013.

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:35.640
Judging by the countless adorable photos of
Everly hanging out on motorcycles on Petko's

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:39.520
Instagram profile, it's clear that he's loving
fatherhood and encouraging his daughter to

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:40.950
follow in his footsteps.

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:44.730
Everly seems to be taking after her father
and looking up to his example.

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:48.680
According to Petko, this girl already understands
the need for speed.

00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:49.980
Petko told Discovery Channel,

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:53.600
"If it's got wheels, she says, 'Go!'"

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:59.390
"I feel the need, the need for speed."

00:00:59.390 --> 00:01:00.840
Jumping networks

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:06.490
After American Chopper was cancelled in 2012,
OCC wasn't quite done being featured on reality

00:01:06.490 --> 00:01:07.490
TV.

00:01:07.490 --> 00:01:12.830
A spinoff of the popular series, simply titled
Orange County Choppers, aired on CMT from

00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:16.390
2013 through 2014, and Petko continued on
as a cast member.

00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:21.140
Orange County Choppers filled a void for dedicated
fans of American Chopper, but the series was

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:23.190
short-lived, running for just one season.

00:01:23.190 --> 00:01:27.400
It was a similar concept to American Chopper
but just didn't carry the same appeal.

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:31.390
It wasn't quite the same without Senior and
Junior's fights keeping things interesting.

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:35.810
It was nice for fans who weren't quite ready
to say goodbye to Senior, Petko, and the rest

00:01:35.810 --> 00:01:39.920
of the crew, but it was missing the exciting
dynamics between cast members that made the

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:41.030
original so entertaining.

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:42.100
Building Shaq's Bike

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:46.020
After Orange County Choppers ended, some of
the American Chopper cast members reunited

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:51.180
in 2014 for a Discovery Channel special titled
American Chopper: Shaq Bike.

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:54.030
Unfortunately, not everyone was back on board
for it.

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:56.650
Petko made an appearance, but there was no
sign of Junior.

00:01:56.650 --> 00:02:00.830
The special was about the crew building a
custom bike for Shaquille O'Neal, and while

00:02:00.830 --> 00:02:03.170
it was a challenge, the crew really stepped
up.

00:02:03.170 --> 00:02:07.670
Shaq's custom made bike, nicknamed the "Man
of Steel," turned out to be the biggest in

00:02:07.670 --> 00:02:09.249
OCC history.

00:02:09.249 --> 00:02:11.340
This bike featured a 48-inch handlebar, a
6-inch rake, a 23-inch front wheel, and a

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:12.340
20-inch rear wheel.

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:15.980
"He's like a little kid that happens to be
seven foot tall."

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:20.329
Until the American Chopper revival started
airing, this was the last time viewers saw

00:02:20.329 --> 00:02:23.239
the crew at OCC appear together onscreen.

00:02:23.239 --> 00:02:27.370
In following years, Petko made some pretty
serious changes in his life and career.

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:31.409
They would take him down a new path that diverged
from the rest of the cast and crew from American

00:02:31.409 --> 00:02:32.409
Chopper.

00:02:32.409 --> 00:02:33.409
A long commute

00:02:33.409 --> 00:02:36.939
Plenty of people can relate to Petko's frustration
with his long commute, which he put up with

00:02:36.939 --> 00:02:39.150
for years while working at OCC.

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:44.000
Three hours in the car each day took away
from time spent with family, enjoying hobbies,

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:45.459
or simply relaxing.

00:02:45.459 --> 00:02:49.360
Fans of American Chopper were well aware of
Petko's extended traveling times, since he

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:53.090
mentioned it plenty of times on the show,
and although he pushed through it for over

00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:55.370
a decade, it clearly began to wear him down.

00:02:55.370 --> 00:02:58.819
"You know, Rick's one of those guys, he doesn't
really say a lot.

00:02:58.819 --> 00:03:03.930
But every day, he drives to OCC about two
hours each way from Pennsylvania."

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:08.749
One reason that Petko left OCC was because
he wanted to spend less time in his car and

00:03:08.749 --> 00:03:12.809
more time closer to home, doing what he really
loved and engaging with his local community.

00:03:12.809 --> 00:03:15.909
It also made life a lot easier for his family.

00:03:15.909 --> 00:03:20.269
Once American Chopper ended and Petko became
a dad, he began to think seriously about working

00:03:20.269 --> 00:03:21.359
closer to home.

00:03:21.359 --> 00:03:25.400
This was always part of his plan, even though
it took several years for him to jump ship

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:26.400
from OCC.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:27.400
His own shop

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:32.249
In 2016, Petko opened his own fabrication
shop in Stroudsburg, Pennsylvania, in conjunction

00:03:32.249 --> 00:03:34.900
with the Pocono Mountain Harley-Davidson dealership.

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:39.409
It all started in December 2015, when Petko
entered a partnership with the dealership's

00:03:39.409 --> 00:03:40.409
management.

00:03:40.409 --> 00:03:44.099
According to Petko, they were super enthusiastic
about working together from the moment that

00:03:44.099 --> 00:03:46.150
he approached them, which took him by surprise.

00:03:46.150 --> 00:03:50.219
It's rare for American dealerships to include
fabrication work in their shops.

00:03:50.219 --> 00:03:54.339
Knowing him personally as a hard worker and
a stand up guy, the dealership managers knew

00:03:54.339 --> 00:03:57.279
that bringing Petko into the business would
be a huge boost.

00:03:57.279 --> 00:04:01.659
Now, customers can essentially build their
custom dream bikes through the dealership,

00:04:01.659 --> 00:04:04.029
and Petko's partnership generated publicity.

00:04:04.029 --> 00:04:08.650
Petko is clearly happy with his new full-time
gig and the possibilities that it presents.

00:04:08.650 --> 00:04:09.839
Petko told the Pocono Record:

00:04:09.839 --> 00:04:13.519
"It has really anything we need to make anything
for anyone's Harley.

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:15.620
If they can dream it up, we can build it.

00:04:15.620 --> 00:04:16.620
That's the main goal."

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:17.620
Other business

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:19.739
Petko's talents are not limited to working
on bikes.

00:04:19.739 --> 00:04:23.830
He has plenty of other interests, and now
that he is not working full time for OCC,

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:26.110
he has more time to spend on outside pursuits.

00:04:26.110 --> 00:04:29.350
Petko's shop, RPD &amp; Co., runs out of his home.

00:04:29.350 --> 00:04:33.240
Through his shop, Petko does metalwork, handforging,
and custom knifework.

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:37.140
As Petko explains on his personal website,
he was originally interested in metalwork

00:04:37.140 --> 00:04:38.810
long before going on TV.

00:04:38.810 --> 00:04:43.110
Yes, his true passion is building motorcycles,
but that's not all he loves to do.

00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:45.050
He actually went to welding school.

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:49.080
Eventually, he went to work as an industrial
contractor, relining kilns and furnaces for

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:50.080
a living.

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:53.920
Now, his business specializes in handmade
culinary knives, and he takes custom orders.

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:56.980
He often shares recent knifework that he's
proud of on Instagram.

00:04:57.620 --> 00:05:07.040
"I was actually coming up with a new blade shape. I was going for something like a train, a high-speed train."

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:08.140
Custom wedding bands

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:12.890
Petko's latest project is creating custom
wedding bands for RPD &amp; Co. customers.

00:05:12.890 --> 00:05:16.440
Wedding bands are the perfect opportunity
for him to get creative with his metalwork.

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:20.220
Petko only takes custom orders for wedding
bands, working with customers to create a

00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:22.110
band that is a symbol of their love.

00:05:22.110 --> 00:05:26.510
There's no doubt that it would cost a little
extra to hire Petko for a custom wedding band,

00:05:26.510 --> 00:05:31.120
but for big fans of American Chopper who like
his artistic style, it might be worth the

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:32.120
price.

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:33.430
After all, a wedding band is meant to last
for life.

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:34.430
"Um actually I did.

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:35.430
I was coming up with actually a new blade
shape when this situation came up.

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:36.430
I was going for something almost like a train,
like a high-speed train."

00:05:36.430 --> 00:05:37.430
Second daughter arrives

00:05:37.430 --> 00:05:38.430
Petko and Cockeram's second child, Lucy, was
born in 2016.

00:05:38.430 --> 00:05:42.400
Like her older sister Everly, she seems to
love hanging out in the bike shop and spending

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:43.400
time with her dad.

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:48.800
Petko supports his daughters by encouraging
them in one of their favorite sports, taekwondo.

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:51.950
Petko is enthusiastic about fatherhood and
putting his family first.

00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:55.950
Viewers of American Chopper will remember
that he was always one of the most down-to-earth

00:05:55.950 --> 00:05:57.140
members of the cast.

00:05:57.140 --> 00:06:01.060
He kept his head down, focused on his work,
and prioritized what really mattered.

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:05.110
It's likely that his new responsibilities
as a father were one of the reasons he keeps

00:06:05.110 --> 00:06:06.920
a lower profile these days.

00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:10.200
Spending time with his wife and daughters
is clearly number one on his list, and being

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:13.900
a reality TV star isn't always conducive to
being a family man.

00:06:13.900 --> 00:06:14.900
Shunning the spotlight

00:06:14.900 --> 00:06:16.990
Petko is a relatively private person.

00:06:16.990 --> 00:06:21.180
Anyone who watched American Chopper will know
that he was never in it for the fame and fortune.

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:24.740
He was just along for the ride, and he was
never too attached to the idea of becoming

00:06:24.740 --> 00:06:26.920
a bona fide "reality TV star."

00:06:26.920 --> 00:06:30.500
He does his job for the love of it, as evidenced
by the fact that he has continued in the same

00:06:30.500 --> 00:06:33.050
line of work even after the cameras stopped
rolling.

00:06:33.050 --> 00:06:34.840
He shows no signs of stopping.

00:06:34.840 --> 00:06:39.710
The very qualities that made Petko so endearing
to audiences, like his laid back, low maintenance

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:44.331
attitude in comparison to other reality TV
stars, is probably why he's not vying to be

00:06:44.331 --> 00:06:45.920
in front of the camera anymore.

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:47.520
He doesn't crave the attention.

00:06:47.520 --> 00:06:51.610
He's had a pretty good run on the small screen,
and now, he's happy to turn over a new leaf

00:06:51.610 --> 00:06:53.460
and seek out different opportunities.

00:06:53.460 --> 00:06:55.950
Petko told the Pocono Record of his time on
American Chopper:

00:06:55.950 --> 00:07:00.639
"That was great while it lasted, but it still
wasn't the core of what I was about or what

00:07:00.639 --> 00:07:01.639
I like to do."

00:07:01.639 --> 00:07:02.639
Sons of Speed

00:07:02.639 --> 00:07:06.440
Even so, Petko appeared on the web series
Sons of Speed for the Motor Trend network

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:07.530
in 2017.

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:12.730
The series followed Billy Lane, who also builds
motorcycles, and his good friend Xavier Murray,

00:07:12.730 --> 00:07:15.860
in their quest to revive the era of board
track racing.

00:07:15.860 --> 00:07:20.620
Lane is an avid collector of motorcycle engines
built in the early 20th century, and his goal

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:23.340
is to restore them and bring them back to
the race track.

00:07:23.340 --> 00:07:28.240
In Sons of Speed, Lane and Murray were preparing
for an upcoming race at the New Smyrna Speedway

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:29.400
in Florida.

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:33.200
It's a limited series of only two episodes,
so fans of American Chopper looking for similar

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:36.040
shows can easily finish watching it in one
night.

00:07:36.040 --> 00:07:39.560
Petko's part in the show involved working
on a specific bike for Lane.

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:43.440
He was interested in the project because it
meant that he would get to work with older

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:45.770
bikes, which has always been one of his passions.

00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:46.770
Petko said,

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:48.260
"I've always had a thing for older bikes.

00:07:48.260 --> 00:07:51.840
It's like a resurgence, it seems like, with
a lot of people just wanting to bring back

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:52.840
these bikes.

00:07:52.840 --> 00:07:56.090
To go a hundred miles per hour on a hundred
year old bike is kind of cool."

00:07:56.090 --> 00:08:00.620
The miniseries was a relatively low key commitment,
which is probably another reason why Petko

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:01.620
chose to partake.

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:02.620
Sitting out the revival

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:06.160
After being off the air for several years,
American Chopper returned to the Discovery

00:08:06.160 --> 00:08:08.620
Channel with a brand new season in 2018.

00:08:08.620 --> 00:08:12.690
A full decade after their business partnership
crumbled, Senior and Junior were running their

00:08:12.690 --> 00:08:16.960
own shops, but they were finally ready to
set aside their differences and work together

00:08:16.960 --> 00:08:18.270
on camera again.

00:08:18.270 --> 00:08:22.080
"The biggest issue me and Paulie had was working
together.

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:25.270
So working on this Yankee bike is a little
strange.

00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:28.150
It kinda brings back some bad memories."

00:08:28.150 --> 00:08:32.190
Longtime fans were definitely excited to see
many of their old favorite cast members, but

00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:34.269
not everyone returned for the revival.

00:08:34.269 --> 00:08:38.089
Petko was notably missing from the two most
recent seasons, and while there is always

00:08:38.089 --> 00:08:42.479
a chance that he could make a surprise appearance,
he hasn't hinted at it, and it seems unlikely.

00:08:42.479 --> 00:08:46.029
He's got a lot on his plate right now, and
it seems like he would rather just keep the

00:08:46.029 --> 00:08:47.529
door closed on American Chopper.

00:08:47.529 --> 00:08:51.459
Petko's fans will always be able to check
in on him and see what he's been working on,

00:08:51.459 --> 00:08:55.820
but when he said that reality TV was not his
major objective, he meant it.

00:08:55.820 --> 00:08:57.050
We'll never say never.

00:08:57.050 --> 00:09:00.810
It's not unthinkable that Petko could pay
a visit to his friends at OCC one day while

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:01.810
the cameras are rolling.

00:09:01.810 --> 00:09:04.920
But for now, it's safe to say that American
Chopper is behind him.

00:09:04.920 --> 00:09:05.920
Races and bike shows

00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:09.920
Petko may not be on TV anymore, but fans who
want to see what he's up to can easily catch

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:11.200
him on Instagram.

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:14.600
He's very open about his latest projects and
updates on his family life.

00:09:14.600 --> 00:09:18.670
While he is clearly very involved with his
own community in Stroudsburg, he also has

00:09:18.670 --> 00:09:20.899
plenty of work commitments all around the
country.

00:09:20.899 --> 00:09:25.720
Petko travels for bike shows and races, and
when possible, he likes to bring his family

00:09:25.720 --> 00:09:26.790
along with him.

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:31.680
For example, in October 2018, he shared that
he was traveling down to the Tennessee Motorcycle

00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:36.610
Revival to show his Indian racer in the Bling's
Cycles Bike Show and ride the bike in the

00:09:36.610 --> 00:09:37.610
Flathead race.

00:09:37.610 --> 00:09:41.850
Petko has also shared that he is looking forward
to participating in the Sons of Speed event

00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:42.850
again.

00:09:42.850 --> 00:09:45.779
He's always updating his fans on new bikes
that he's working on and whether or not he'll

00:09:45.779 --> 00:09:47.149
be getting them out on the track.

00:09:47.149 --> 00:09:51.430
He knows that although his audience can't
tune in to see him on TV anymore, they are

00:09:51.430 --> 00:09:55.350
still interested in the bikes that he's constructing
and where he's headed next.

00:09:55.350 --> 00:09:57.110
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:09:57.110 --> 00:10:00.370
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
shows are coming soon.

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:03.260
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

